    {
      "id": "Aldb74uei7I_Rs7v2A8T2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 416,
      "y": 203.5,
      "width": 930.7391357421875,
      "height": 1000,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b38",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1324413701,
      "version": 1184,
      "versionNonce": 1066172395,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788773556237,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Design whatsapp\n\n- whatsapp is a messaging service that allows users to send and receive encrypted \nmessages and calls from their phones and computers. whatsapp was famously originally\nbuild on Erlang and renowned for handling high scale with limited engineering and infrastructure \n\n\nFunctional Requirements\n\n- start group chats\n- send/receive messages \n- send/receive media \n- access message after i have been offline \n\nNon functional requirements \n\n- low latency \n- guarantee delivery messages \n- billions of users, high throughput \n- messages not stored unnecessarily\n- fault tolerant \n- consistency \n\nCore Entities \n\n- user\n- chat\n- messages\n- client \n\n\nCommands Sent      Commands received\n\n   create chat          newmessage \n  send message               chatupdate \n    createAttachment \n    modify participants \n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Design whatsapp\n\n- whatsapp is a messaging service that allows users to send and receive encrypted \nmessages and calls from their phones and computers. whatsapp was famously originally\nbuild on Erlang and renowned for handling high scale with limited engineering and infrastructure \n\n\nFunctional Requirements\n\n- start group chats\n- send/receive messages \n- send/receive media \n- access message after i have been offline \n\nNon functional requirements \n\n- low latency \n- guarantee delivery messages \n- billions of users, high throughput \n- messages not stored unnecessarily\n- fault tolerant \n- consistency \n\nCore Entities \n\n- user\n- chat\n- messages\n- client \n\n\nCommands Sent      Commands received\n\n   create chat          newmessage \n  send message               chatupdate \n    createAttachment \n    modify participants \n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
